inl runtime_drift_burndown () = Task ("SPI-RUNTIME-DRIFT-BURNDOWN", "Burn down RustGlobal as real implementation debt rather than treating runtime-file renames as completion: toolchain actions, checkpoints, outcomes, payloads, profiles, programs, environment keys and modes, receipt protocol fields, and source identity policy now derive from explicit Spiral unions and exhaustive mappings; generated policy and probe remain byte-identical while the monolithic catalog string is retired. Toolchain decimal parsing for receipt fields, timeout input and portable identity byte counts now reuses the shared Spiral state_receipt_codec_core with explicit u64/u32/i32 bounds; v211 regenerates the owner from a byte-identical predecessor baseline, focused tests are six-of-six green, and Clippy is warning-free. Rust still owns physical metadata traversal, receipt filesystem IO, sibling-path checks, concrete environment effects, process launch, streams, termination and narrow numeric transport. Agile SeriesRecord and MigrationDenominator u32 decoding now consumes the same shared state_receipt_codec_core as a Cargo dependency; the codec residualizes once as a 912-line generated core in a 961-line Cargo crate while its lexical model lives in a package-only sibling and eoie-agile-state is 572 generated Rust LOC; u32 suffix, source-tag dash shape, MigrationDenominator constructor/payload framing, and SeriesRecord discovery/payload/append-only sequence validation are Spiral-owned; an independent thirteen-case lexical package main proves tag, constructor, stream, duplicate-sequence, and malformed-record edges, and the global crate ceiling stays at 997. Bundle ZIP is MappingActive: package-only Spiral now owns profile names and codes, minimal EOIE archive signature, canonical root entries, the stricter hydrated-root Agile requirement, crate source extensions, and the crate auxiliary-file whitelist. Positive strict rehydrate, missing-Agile, forbidden-root-file, and missing-evidence negative fixtures stay fail-closed; the bundle owner shrinks from seven-hundred-twenty-one to seven-hundred-fourteen generated Rust LOC while the reusable manifest owner grows six, yielding net minus one generated Rust LOC across touched Cargo owners. Top-level source, state, evidence, crate, size, extraction, density, public-binary, vendor, archive-root and forbidden-lib.rs policies are now consumed from package-only Spiral; profile resolution is single-generated, archive-manifest parity is shared through eoie-bundle-manifest, and semantic closeout now consumes the migration observed from typed state instead of a duplicated numeric literal in the bundle terminal. Bundle ZIP now delegates semantic text reads plus crate, state, source and vendor traversal to the shared descriptor-relative nofollow filesystem authority; the generated bundle owner has zero direct fs::read_dir, fs::symlink_metadata or fs::read_to_string sites and a state-witness symlink fixture fails closed. Archive input paths now fail closed on symlinks before ZIP open; rehydration order is now an indexed Spiral plan whose preflight, extraction, validation and commit bindings consume observed archive and profile facts, while archive regular-file creation, symlink/hardlink creation, staging creation/promotion and rollback now consume the shared descriptor-relative mutation boundary across ZIP and TAR; archive ZIP input opening now consumes the shared descriptor-relative nofollow regular-file read boundary and rejects symlinked input paths at the actual open; directory-mode mutation now consumes the shared descriptor-relative directory-mode boundary and rejects symlinked ancestors before chmod; archive tree validation now consumes shared descriptor-relative directory listing, symlink reads and regular-file opens, hardlink target classification reuses the same regular-open boundary, and archive_deflate_domain has no direct fs::read_dir, fs::symlink_metadata or fs::read_link sites. Bundle create and verify now obtain ZIP file size through the shared descriptor-relative nofollow regular-file boundary instead of path metadata; the new ELF verifies the published predecessor and creates plus verifies a clean-root bundle before closeout. Live handoff ratings census toolchain ColdProof section and Active-work parsing now execute in four narrow Spiral-authored projection domains; the Rust handoff terminal only reads files, invokes generated projections, validates envelopes, orders output and formats presentation labels. Splitting Active work and handoff sections into independent owners preserves the one-thousand-line crate and Rust-file ceiling while the physical rust_global helper-site count falls from two-thousand-one-hundred-nine to two-thousand-sixty; the count remains a secondary census; task progress records semantic extraction credit rather than site-count gaming. Bundle ZIP coverage witness interpretation now reuses the package-only state receipt codec model: durable missing and absent checkpoint declarations plus the expected SHA are Spiral-owned and independently probed; the bundle Rust keeps only physical coverage-state reads checkpoint existence nofollow hashing and byte comparison. The bundle owner is reproducible again under v212 after package-only consumers were corrected from the main-bearing codec crate to the reusable codec model, while the shared codec crate remains exactly one-thousand physical LOC. Bundle create-flat and verify-flat max-bytes decimal parsing now delegates to the shared Spiral u64 receipt codec; bundle Rust retains only error mapping and physical archive-size enforcement. Recovered capability and dogfood topology-count assignments now use a dedicated Spiral-generated state-recovered-topology-codec over the shared package-only lexical model; bundle Rust keeps physical recovered-fixture enumeration, evidence-path existence checks and count comparison, while assignment lookup, u32 suffix validation, decimal decoding, overflow and missing/malformed classification are Spiral-owned; the independent lexical probe covers positive fixture, positive dogfood, missing and malformed assignment cases, and the new residual stays far below the one-thousand-line ceiling. The same topology codec now owns recovered-fixture row shape, record count, duplicate-capability rejection and normalized evidence-path projection, leaving Rust with physical nofollow path checks; workspace Cargo member uniqueness also moved into the Spiral manifest parser while Rust only materializes the already validated set. EOIE archive root-shape conjunction now uses a v213-regenerated Spiral bitmask binding; Rust observes only exact/prefix presence in physical ZIP entries. Post-rehydrate structure validity now also uses the topology codec: Rust reports EOIE signature, Agile-file and generic-manifest presence as a compact mask while Spiral owns the profile-dependent acceptance rule; direct residualization in bundle_zip was rejected by the density gate and the shared topology residual keeps the global crate ceiling at 997. EOIE profile signature acceptance for live roots and archive entries now delegates two physical presence masks to the Spiral topology codec; the four required paths remain emitted by bundle_policy_domain, the source-matched v213 release ELF is promoted transactionally, and public contracts pass fourteen-of-fourteen. Agile attestation action selection now delegates module-kind plus compact same-content/compiler/build observations to a typed Spiral decision union; static drift remains fail-closed without a compiler, build-attests with one, and transient receipt drift runtime-attests without one. Transient receipt schema/name and state-path candidacy, record preflight, mutation-target authorization, lease-budget/readback acceptance, prompt-title and Task-line classification, Agile status-name serialization, snapshot/module receipt row-kind decode/emit labels, and runtime/build receipt-attestation wire classification plus canonical emission, and PromptLease marker/status/shape plus WORK-WRAP-YIELD phase selection are now compiled Spiral policy; canonical Spiral string escaping for prompt/task/history mutations and state package.spiproj lexical header/comment/boundary/module normalization are also Spiral-owned; tuple and serializer now declare direct state_receipt_codec_model ownership, and shared receipt-attestation kind, build-payload extraction and canonical wire semantics live in that package-only codec model for both runtime policy and serializer, while Rust retains physical filesystem and clock observations, prompt tuple slicing and numeric decode, sequential module-section traversal, BTreeMap and narrow numeric transport, atomic receipt IO, and effect execution.", Epic, P0, D8, 86u32, Active, "SPI-RUNTIME-DRIFT-INVENTORY", "runtime,rustglobal,mapping,compiler,pillars,type-truth", "next", "current")
inl toolchain_runtime_policy_burndown () = Task ("TOOLCHAIN-RUNTIME-POLICY-BURNDOWN", "Move toolchain checkpoint execution eligibility and physical timeout success failure outcome classification into the independent compiled Spiral toolchain_runtime_policy_domain; regenerate the proxy through v198, prove the policy executable plus focused tests and Clippy, keep manual Rust at zero, and preserve the one-thousand-line topology ceiling while owner-growth records two-hundred-sixteen growth versus six-hundred-forty-seven shrink.", Story, P0, D5, 100u32, Done, "SPI-RUNTIME-DRIFT-BURNDOWN", "toolchain,rustglobal,policy,spiral,shrinkage", "next", "current")
