inl recovered_prototype_metric_retirement () = Task ("RECOVERED-PROTOTYPE-METRIC-RETIREMENT", "Keep recovered prototype maturity only as retired historical V1 evidence and exclude it from the active progress panel", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "RATING-CODEBASE-REBASELINE", "ratings,historical,retired,v1", "current", "settled")
inl parallel_readiness_reassessment () = Task ("PARALLEL-READINESS-REASSESSMENT", "Parallel readiness is re-opened as an active measured workstream: deterministic fifty-six-worker search, manifest parity, parallel state checks and coverage are proved, while general work pulling, bounded multi-owner scheduling and broader concurrent product execution remain unfinished. Completion now requires a physical benchmark that demonstrates CPU saturation without starving supervision or violating the lease.", Story, P1, D6, 70u32, Active, "COVERAGE-COMPARABLE-REFRESH", "parallel,ratings,decision,scheduler,benchmark", "next", "current")
inl active_codebase_regauge () = Task ("RATING-ACTIVE-CODEBASE-REGUAGE", "Re-anchor ProjectSota to the weighted active-phase denominator five-hundred-fifty-three and publish eight-hundred-fifty as the maximum admissible subjective ceiling. This settlement deliberately applies large negative deltas to fruitfulness, satisfaction, EOIE SOTA, workflow, Spiral authority, verification, handoff, toolchain, runtime-drift visibility, definition stability and state hygiene; these are calibration corrections against unfinished codebase work, not regressions in settled migration evidence. A first generic compile-time guard experiment failed typecheck and was rolled back, so hard enforcement remains an explicit P0 rather than being falsely claimed.", Story, P0, D4, 100u32, Done, "POST-RETIREMENT-PHASE-DENOMINATOR,POST-RETIREMENT-LEGACY-RECONCILE", "ratings,calibration,truth,active-work", "current", "settled")
inl rating_active_ceiling_gate () = Task ("RATING-ACTIVE-CEILING-GATE", "Make the subjective ceiling executable instead of advisory: every ActiveSignal rating must fail build attestation above eight-hundred-fifty while objective and historical ratings remain exempt. The first generic Rating-union helper did not typecheck and was reverted; retry with a smaller sample-grounded representation before changing production ratings again.", Story, P0, D5, 100u32, Done, "RATING-ACTIVE-CODEBASE-REGUAGE", "ratings,ceiling,typecheck,negative-fixture,anti-inflation", "next", "current")

inl agile_runtime_compiler_independence () = Task ("AGILE-RUNTIME-COMPILER-INDEPENDENCE", "Make deployed Agile operations compiler-independent: begin set record and clean check validate deterministic runtime schemas and state identities inside the binary; the Spiral compiler is consulted only to attest externally modified static state during development, never as a normal deployment prerequisite.", Story, P0, D7, 100u32, Done, "SPI-RUNTIME-DRIFT-BURNDOWN", "agile,deployment,compiler,receipt,runtime,fail-closed", "current", "settled")
inl rustglobal_physical_baseline () = Task ("RUSTGLOBAL-PHYSICAL-BASELINE", "Keep a physical baseline for direct Rust escape debt using deterministic parallel search: current source has eighty-seven files defining rust_global and one-thousand-three-hundred-seventy-nine RustGlobal emissions after four real bridge-or-shadow removals; future burndown credit requires semantic removal or narrowing rather than concatenating strings.", Story, P0, D4, 100u32, Done, "SPI-RUNTIME-DRIFT-INVENTORY", "rustglobal,baseline,physical,anti-gaming", "current", "settled")
inl rustglobal_agile_boundary () = Task ("RUSTGLOBAL-AGILE-BOUNDARY", "Continue shrinking the Agile physical boundary after compiler independence: shared package-only agile_mutation_policy now owns progress/status acceptance, the exact eleven-field Task shape, Task identity acceptance, receipt content freshness, build-fingerprint currentness, and topology snapshot acceptance. Rust only parses, escapes, measures, and serializes physical data for these decisions. Negative fixtures prove mutation rejection and receipt drift fail-closed with compiler reattestation. This cut moves tuple parsing, receipt attestation syntax, legacy receipt migration, and runtime/build attestation token validation into compiled Spiral. Rust now keeps only narrow filesystem, clock, environment, process, numeric conversion, and transport duties for this path. This cut additionally moves prompt lease decimal/u64 parsing, canonical u64 literal parsing, receipt numeric-field decoding, and build-attestation fingerprint decoding behind compiled Spiral codecs. Malformed and overflowing u64 values now fail closed before state mutation. Exact snapshot/module row framing now lives in the dedicated state_receipt_tuple_domain runtime owner and malformed or tab-ambiguous rows fail closed before the Rust adapter transports fields. Rust retains only narrow filesystem, clock, environment, process, escaping, measurement, serialization, and final field transport duties. The final cut exports the five-string receipt tuple through the Spiral compiler, proves portable refcount batch lowering and generated wrapper lint cleanliness, and removes the remaining Rust field split. Agile receipt meaning is now fully Spiral-owned; Rust retains only physical filesystem, clock, environment, process, escaping, measurement, serialization, and typed field transport duties.", Story, P0, D7, 100u32, Done, "AGILE-RUNTIME-COMPILER-INDEPENDENCE,RUSTGLOBAL-PHYSICAL-BASELINE", "rustglobal,agile,boundary,spiral,type-truth", "next", "current")
inl evidence_chain_currentness () = Task ("EVIDENCE-CHAIN-CURRENTNESS", "Make bundle verification prove current evidence instead of accepting shape-only sidecars: typed EvidenceRef now manifests eighteen current proofs, with sixteen file identities plus an exact whole-src tree digest and a whole-state digest that excludes only the two self-observing meta-manifests state/evidence.spi and state/typecheck_receipts.spi. Live status recomputes both tree hashes, rejects drift fail-closed, and remains compilerless at deployment. Whole-tree currentness is complete; preserve it through every closeout.", Epic, P0, D8, 100u32, Done, "COVERAGE-CHECKPOINT-DURABILITY", "evidence,receipt,hash,currentness,bundle,fail-closed,tree", "current", "settled")
inl cold_build_toolchain_identity () = Task ("COLD-BUILD-TOOLCHAIN-IDENTITY", "Pin the Spiral compiler and Rust toolchain identity and prove source-to-residual-to-binary reconstruction in an otherwise empty environment; deployment must not require either compiler. Compiler attestation identity remains transitive over wrapper plus facade. The empty-root campaign now derives all ninety source-to-target pairs automatically, deletes and regenerates all ninety outputs without matrix edits, and builds a release binary from a fresh Cargo target offline. Compiler v196 remains authority. Multi-output provenance is fail-closed and now resolves semantic roles plus canonical [lib] ownership; rust_std_fs and toolchain_command_domain close without manual pairing. The epic is cold-proven and complete.", Epic, P0, D8, 100u32, Done, "AGILE-RUNTIME-COMPILER-INDEPENDENCE", "build,compiler,toolchain,identity,cold,reproducibility", "next", "current")
inl deployment_compiler_dependency_cut () = Task ("DEPLOYMENT-COMPILER-DEPENDENCY-CUT", "Audit and remove post-build compiler expectations from deployable EOIE operations beyond Agile. Agile, patch, retention, binary provenance, release closeout and normal Cargo toolchain receipts are compilerless and runtime-validated; remaining source-author and prune-uncovered compiler paths are build-authoring operations that must be explicitly classified in CLI/help before closing this epic.", Epic, P0, D8, 100u32, Done, "AGILE-RUNTIME-COMPILER-INDEPENDENCE", "deployment,compiler,runtime,patch,prune,provenance,receipt", "next", "current")

inl canonical_plan_ir () = Task ("CANONICAL-PLAN-IR", "Replace line-oriented reparsing of Spiral patch and batch source with a compiler-produced canonical typed plan representation so physical executors consume explicit enums newtypes results and witnesses rather than searching source text.", Epic, P0, D8, 0u32, Planned, "RUSTGLOBAL-PHYSICAL-BASELINE", "compiler,ir,plan,parser,witness,type-truth", "future", "planned")
inl physical_boundary_hardening () = Task ("PHYSICAL-BOUNDARY-HARDENING", "Harden the remaining OS boundary with unpredictable exclusive temporaries, ancestor-symlink confinement, bounded process output and explicit platform capability checks. This cut extends physical hardening through three narrow terminals: central filesystem staging uses pid-plus-time nonces with create_new and sync_all; rooted path resolution rejects existing symlink ancestors and patch_control delegates to the same rust_std_fs authority instead of maintaining a divergent parser; process capture bounds each stdout/stderr stream at sixteen MiB by default with an explicit sixty-four MiB ceiling and kills/reaps the child on overflow. Negative fixtures prove ancestor traversal and output overflow fail closed. This cut also makes copy staging exclusive through the shared nonce create_new writer, rejects replacement where rename-over-existing is not an explicit platform capability, and places bounded Unix children in their own process group so timeout, output overflow, and callback abort signal the group and direct child before reaping. A grandchild-survival fixture proves the stale direct-child behavior leaves a marker while the rebuilt candidate does not. This cut now opens rooted regular files descriptor-relative on Unix and applies no-follow at every ancestor and at the final leaf; generated negative tests prove both ancestor and leaf symlink substitution fail closed. Process supervision also publishes an explicit platform capability and non-Unix direct-child-only execution fails closed instead of claiming process-tree authority. The current cut extracts mutating filesystem authority into rust_std_fs_mutation: Linux atomic staging and promotion, copy, unlink and recursive removal now use descriptor-relative openat, renameat and unlinkat with no-follow, and generated negative tests cover symlink ancestors, parent-swap race and tree-removal escape. rust_std_fs stays a narrow facade; the split preserves the one-thousand-line crate ceiling and shrinks generated Rust. This cut also promotes eoie_process_streaming from package-only injection to its own generated Rust crate, moves timeout policy and process-tree signaling into that narrow owner, and initially leaves eoie-process as a 247-line facade over a 350-line streaming owner; the current public run_bounded consolidation reduces the facade to 233 generated Rust LOC while the streaming owner remains 350. Focused check, tests, Clippy and all fourteen public contracts pass; a cold focused check measured 11.00 seconds on the predecessor and 11.27 seconds on the candidate, so ParallelReadiness receives no credit. This cut also closes two previously hidden same-platform gaps: rooted directory listing now enumerates through the already-open Linux descriptor instead of reopening the path, with a path-swap fixture proving descriptor binding; non-Linux rooted reads fail closed instead of racing symlink_metadata against File::open. The public run_bounded path now delegates to eoie_process_streaming, so timeout, output overflow and callback abort share process-group tree termination rather than the former direct-child loop; a grandchild marker fixture proves public timeout kills the descendant tree. Remaining work is native non-Linux descriptor-relative read and mutation parity plus native non-Unix process-tree supervision where supported; keep these effects in narrow Rust terminals rather than semantic owners.", Epic, P1, D8, 98u32, Active, "RUSTGLOBAL-PHYSICAL-BASELINE", "filesystem,process,symlink,temp,security,boundary,exclusive-create", "current", "current")

inl process_supervision_owner_split () = Task ("PROCESS-SUPERVISION-OWNER-SPLIT", "Promote eoie_process_streaming from package-only injection to an independent Spiral-generated crate, give timeout policy its own compiled binding, keep process-tree signaling in the narrow physical streaming terminal, and reexport the public process API from eoie-process. The old eoie-process residual shrinks from 998 to 247 LOC while the new streaming owner is 350 LOC; focused Cargo check, tests, Clippy and fourteen public contracts pass. Cold focused Cargo check is 11.00 seconds on the predecessor versus 11.27 seconds on the candidate, so the structural split earns no ParallelReadiness score increase.", Story, P0, D6, 100u32, Done, "PHYSICAL-BOUNDARY-HARDENING", "process,streaming,crate,split,spiral,shrinkage", "current", "current")

inl filesystem_descriptor_listing_hardening () = Task ("FILESYSTEM-DESCRIPTOR-LISTING-HARDENING", "Bind rooted directory enumeration to the already-open Linux directory descriptor, reject the previous path-reopen race, make non-Linux rooted reads fail closed instead of symlink-check then open, and prove a rename-plus-symlink path swap cannot redirect the held descriptor listing.", Story, P0, D5, 100u32, Done, "PHYSICAL-BOUNDARY-HARDENING", "filesystem,descriptor,list,race,linux,fail-closed", "current", "current")

inl process_public_tree_timeout () = Task ("PROCESS-PUBLIC-TREE-TIMEOUT", "Route the public run_bounded path through eoie_process_streaming so timeout, output overflow and callback abort share process-group tree supervision; preserve streamed stdout and stderr and prove a delayed grandchild marker cannot survive the public timeout.", Story, P0, D5, 100u32, Done, "PHYSICAL-BOUNDARY-HARDENING,PROCESS-SUPERVISION-OWNER-SPLIT", "process,tree,timeout,streaming,grandchild,public", "current", "current")

inl rust_bootstrap_order_recovery () = Task ("BOOT-RUST-PROOF-ORDER-RECOVERY", "Record the protocol miss where source edits were applied before this round proved the local Rust installer; those edits remained unpromoted until the installer, Cargo, tests and Clippy passed. Future rounds must prove Rust before the first source mutation rather than recovering after it.", TaskKind, P0, D2, 100u32, Done, "BOOT-MANUAL-SESSION-LEASE", "bootstrap,rust,order,recovery", "current", "current")

inl lease_absolute_clock () = Task ("LEASE-ABSOLUTE-CLOCK", "Persist prompt start, wrap and deadline timestamps and surface remaining_ms plus should_wrap and should_yield from agile check so the seventy-five minute semantic-work boundary, ten minute closeout guard and eighty-five-minute hard deadline are enforced distinctly by EOIE instead of manual wall clock alone", Story, P0, D5, 100u32, Done, "", "workflow,lease,timebox,spiral,non-migration", "current", "current")

inl optional_compiler_discovery () = Task ("OPTIONAL-COMPILER-DISCOVERY", "Resolve an optional Spiral compiler generically with strict precedence explicit argument then EOIE_SPIRAL_COMPILE then host-local XDG or HOME config then PATH; clean deployment remains compilerless, while compiler presence upgrades runtime receipts to build attestations keyed by compiler fingerprint and checkpoints each module for resumable first-time promotion.", Story, P0, D7, 100u32, Done, "AGILE-RUNTIME-COMPILER-INDEPENDENCE,COLD-BUILD-TOOLCHAIN-IDENTITY", "compiler,discovery,config,attestation,deployment,resume", "current", "settled")
inl unbounded_count_topology () = Task ("UNBOUNDED-COUNT-TOPOLOGY", "Remove ceilings on the number of state files Cargo crates Spiral packages and projects; preserve only local source-size guards of at most one-thousand LOC per Rust file and per Cargo crate. A sixty-four-state-file scratch bundle and the seventy-third Cargo crate prove horizontal growth is unbounded.", Story, P0, D5, 100u32, Done, "POST-RETIREMENT-PHASE-DENOMINATOR", "state,crate,package,topology,unbounded,loc", "current", "settled")
inl compiler_tail_loop_return_regression () = Task ("COMPILER-TAIL-LOOP-RETURN-REGRESSION", "Prevent Rust tail-loop lowering from turning non-recursive returns into loop-body tail expressions. PortableBackends source now keeps explicit returns inside tail loops; the bounded _eoie wrapper repairs legacy facade output until the full facade assembly is rebuilt. Both eoie-agile-lease and eoie-agile-mutation regenerate from Spiral and pass focused Cargo checks.", Story, P0, D6, 100u32, Done, "COLD-BUILD-TOOLCHAIN-IDENTITY,COMPILER-MULTI-UNION-AGILE-FIXTURE", "compiler,rust,tail-loop,return,regression,cold", "current", "settled")

inl cold_residual_map_resume () = Task ("COLD-RESIDUAL-MAP-RESUME", "Close the ninety-owner Spiral-to-Rust reconstruction with compiler output canonized before comparison, bounded owner batches, and Cargo proof before promotion. This round closes the final four adjudications: legacy-operations is regenerated at nine-hundred-twenty-five lines once rustfmt uses the workspace max-width policy; evidence-currentness and compiler-discovery are freshly regenerated and gated; the domain probe recompiles byte-identically. The full map is ninety of ninety current and gated, workspace Clippy remains green, and zero manual Rust is authored. Preserve this nominal closeout and move the cold-build epic to the full empty-root reconstruction.", Story, P0, D7, 100u32, Done, "COMPILER-TAIL-LOOP-RETURN-REGRESSION", "compiler,residual,cold,map,batch,owner", "current", "settled")

